{
	"Name": "Okta - Authentication & Sessions - Okta Brute Force Against One Account",
	"Description": "Alert: Okta\nGroup: Authentication & Sessions\nMITRE ATT&CK: Credential Access / T1110.001\nSchedule: every 15 minutes over the previous 15 minutes (edit the scheduled search to change it)\nTuning: okta_user_allowlist / okta_ip_allowlist keys \"<login without domain>|Okta Brute Force Against One Account\" or \"<ip>|Okta Brute Force Against One Account\"\n\nFive or more failed authentications with INVALID_CREDENTIALS (user.session.start or user.authentication.*) for one user within the search window. Replaces a rule that alerted on every failed authentication. Password sprays across many users are covered by the two \"Password Spray\" rules.\n\nFalse positives: a user who forgot a recently changed password; a script with a stale password.\n\nReference(s):\n- https://detection.fyi/elastic/detection-rules/integrations/okta/credential_access_okta_brute_force_or_password_spraying/\n- https://github.com/elastic/detection-rules/blob/main/rules/integrations/okta/credential_access_okta_brute_force_or_password_spraying.toml",
	"GUID": "587fedd0-0aa2-513f-ac33-279ee39a0e5d",
